+### Honest Gaps
+
+The GitHub ecosystem is still thin for narrowly specialized open source ecommerce AI in a few areas:
+
+- Dynamic pricing engines that are clearly AI-first and actively maintained on GitHub are still sparse.
+- Retail-specific returns optimization and claims automation repos are limited.
+- End-to-end merchant copilots with clean open source licensing are fewer than the hype cycle suggests.
+
+Rather than padding the list with SaaS products or loosely related demos, those gaps are left explicit.
+
+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for ecommerce search in 2026?
+For search-heavy use cases, start with `Meilisearch`, `Typesense`, `Qdrant`, `Weaviate`, or `Vespa`. The right choice depends on whether you need classic faceted search, semantic retrieval, or hybrid ranking.
+
+### Which GitHub repos are best for product recommendations in ecommerce?
+`Microsoft Recommenders`, `RecBole`, and `NVIDIA Merlin` are the strongest recommendation-focused repos in this list. `Qdrant`, `Weaviate`, and `Vespa` are also useful when recommendation logic depends on vector similarity or online ranking.
+
+### Are there self-hosted AI chatbots for ecommerce customer support?
+Yes. `Rasa`, `Flowise`, `Langflow`, `Haystack`, and `AnythingLLM` can all be used to build self-hosted support assistants, guided selling flows, and internal commerce copilots.
+
+### What open source AI tools can extract data from supplier catalogs and invoices?
+`PaddleOCR`, `Docling`, `Unstructured`, `docTR`, and `LayoutParser` are the most relevant GitHub repos in this list for catalog ingestion, OCR, and document parsing.
+
+### What are the best GitHub tools for ecommerce product image automation?
+`rembg` is the easiest win for background removal, while `Real-ESRGAN` helps with restoration and upscaling. `InvokeAI`, `Fooocus`, and `Stable Diffusion WebUI` are better for creative generation and editing workflows.
+
+### Can I build an entire ecommerce AI stack from open source GitHub repos?
+Yes, but it is usually a composition problem. A realistic stack might pair `Meilisearch` or `Typesense` with `Qdrant`, use `RecBole` or `Merlin` for recommendations, `Rasa` or `Flowise` for support, and `Docling` plus `PaddleOCR` for ingestion.
+
+### Why are some famous AI ecommerce products missing from this list?
